                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="325-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_sc.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Supercardioid" title="Supercardioid" ></span>AKG Acoustics D 3800</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Supercardioid Dynamic Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The D3800 is a handheld dynamic microphone intended for live vocal reproduction. It uses AKG&#8217;s &#8220;Varimotion&#8221; laminate diaphragm technology, and a triangular &#8220;TriPower&#8221; body.</p><p>The mic&#8217;s moving-coil capsule is suspended within the mic body to reduce mechanical noise. A hum suppression coil helps reduce EMI/RFI (radio or electronic interference).</p><blockquote><p><cite>AKG</cite><p>The VARIMOTION diaphragm is the first microphone diaphragm ever made whose thickness varies across its diameter. This allows the diaphragm itself to be tuned to the desired resonance frequency for a quantum leap in audio performance.</p></p></blockquote><p>The package includes the microphone, a stand adapter and a hard shell road case.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/AKG-Acoustics/D-3800">AKG Acoustics D 3800</a> is also known as: D3800, D 3800.</p>
